This is a rust project; the workspace is every dir in crates/ (root Cargo.toml `members = ["crates/*"]`):
goose: the main code for goose, contains all the core logic (session runtime in src/agents/, ACP server in src/acp/, recipes, hints, plugins, hooks)
goose-agent: the GDK agent loop (state machine in src/machine.rs)
goose-cli: the `goose` binary; `goose serve` is the backend the desktop app spawns (ui/desktop/src/gooseServe.ts)
goose-mcp: the mcp servers that ship with goose (the developer extension itself lives in goose/src/agents/platform_extensions/developer)
goose-providers / goose-provider-types: LLM providers
goose-sdk / goose-sdk-types: the goose Development Kit (GDK); release-plz.toml lists the published GDK crates
also: goose-acp-macros, goose-context-management, goose-download-manager, goose-local-inference, goose-roaming, goose-test, goose-test-support


ui/desktop has an electron app in typescript. It talks to `goose serve` over ACP, not an OpenAPI server: there is no goose-server crate any more.

non trivial features should be implemented in the goose crate and then be called from the goose-cli crate for the cli. for the desktop, add or extend the ACP handlers in
crates/goose/src/acp/server/, then run `just generate-acp-types` to regenerate crates/goose/acp-schema.json and ui/goose-acp-client/src/generated/, and call it from
the typescript through the goose-acp-client package (ui/goose-acp-client). Do not recreate ui/desktop/src/api (see AGENTS.md).

tips:
- can look at unstaged changes for what is being worked on if starting
- always check rust compiles, cargo fmt etc and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` (as well as run tests in files you are working on)
- in ui/desktop, look at how you can run lint checks and if other tests can run

harness/ is this fork's multi-agent harness (no Rust; goose extension points only): read harness/README.md before working there.
